# 🍷 Wine Quality Prediction Using Machine Learning

## 📌 Project Overview

The **Wine Quality Prediction** project uses machine learning classification algorithms to predict wine quality categories based on physicochemical properties such as acidity, density, pH, sulphates, and alcohol content.

The project analyzes a combined dataset containing red and white wine records, explores patterns in the data, and compares three classification models to determine which performs best.

## 🎯 Objectives

* Load and explore the Wine Quality dataset.
* Analyze the distribution of wine quality scores.
* Visualize chemical feature distributions using histograms.
* Examine relationships between numerical features using a correlation heatmap.
* Investigate class imbalance in wine quality categories.
* Group quality scores into Low, Medium, and High categories.
* Split the dataset into training and testing sets using stratification.
* Train and evaluate three machine learning classifiers.
* Compare model performance using evaluation metrics.
* Identify important features using Random Forest feature importance.

